@{
    Layout = "_LayoutLanding";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Security";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How Hermes protects accounts and financial data, and how to report security issues.";
}

<div class="legal-content">
    <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" class="inline-link legal-back">← Back to Hermes</a>

    <h1>Security</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: 24 September 2026</p>

    <p>
        Hermes handles sensitive personal finance information. Security controls are intended to
        protect account access, isolate users’ data, and reduce the risk of unauthorized access,
        while remaining proportionate to the current size and purpose of the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Current safeguards</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Authentication is required to access income, expenses, budgets, goals, and exports.</li>
        <li>Passwords are stored using hashed password management rather than plain text.</li>
        <li>Authentication cookies use secure, HTTP-only, and same-site protections.</li>
        <li>Financial pages are restricted to authenticated users.</li>
        <li>Transactions, categories, budgets, and goals are associated with individual user accounts.</li>
        <li>Application requests use validation and anti-forgery protections where applicable.</li>
        <li>Authentication requests are subject to rate limiting.</li>
        <li>Production traffic is served over HTTPS with HTTP Strict Transport Security enabled.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Operational practices</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Access to production data should be limited to authorized maintenance and support.</li>
        <li>Backups and recovery procedures should be maintained for operational resilience.</li>
        <li>Security updates, dependencies, and configurations should be reviewed regularly.</li>
        <li>Suspicious authentication activity, errors, and abuse reports should be investigated.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Use a strong, unique password for Hermes.</li>
        <li>Do not share your credentials.</li>
        <li>Sign out from shared or public devices.</li>
        <li>Keep your browser and operating system updated.</li>
        <li>Verify financial summaries before making important decisions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Limitations</h2>
    <p>
        No online service can guarantee absolute security. Hermes does not promise protection against
        every possible attack, software vulnerability, credential compromise, device compromise, or
        third-party infrastructure incident. Users should avoid storing credentials or sensitive
        information outside their secure account environment.
    </p>

    <h2>Report a security issue</h2>
    <p>
        Security concerns can be reported through the
        <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/franciscocosta4/Hermes" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hermes GitHub repository</a>.
        Include a clear description, affected pages or actions, reproduction steps, and the date and
        time of the event. Do not include passwords or other users’ personal data.
    </p>
</div>
